              c: "Persian classical poetry — especially the works of Hafez and Rumi — was deeply entwined with the medical tradition, using garden imagery to teach principles of self-care."),
        Quote(q: "Rhodiola grows where the air is thin and the cold is fierce. It teaches us to thrive in difficulty.",
