              c: "This humorous expression reflects a deep trust in herbal wisdom — the recognition that plant intelligence exceeds our current understanding of their mechanisms."),
        Quote(q: "The hands that prepare the medicine must be clean in spirit, not only in water.",
              a: "Curanderismo teaching",
              c: "In Curanderismo, the healer's state of mind and heart during preparation is believed to enter the medicine — mental agitation or negative emotion can diminish its effectiveness."),
        Quote(q: "Yerba santa — sacred herb — opens the lungs, clears grief, and makes space for the new.",
              a: "Chumash and Latino healing tradition",
              c: "Eriodictyon californicum (yerba santa) was used by Native California and later Chicano healing traditions for respiratory ailments and is associated with the clearing of emotional heaviness."),
        Quote(q: "We do not cleanse because we are dirty. We cleanse because we value what we carry.",
              a: "Curanderismo teaching",
              c: "The periodic cleanse in Curanderismo is not punitive but celebratory — an act of self-respect that honors the body as the carrier of ancestral life and spiritual potential."),
        Quote(q: "The river always returns to the sea. Let your healing cycle be like the river.",
              a: "Andean healing tradition",
              c: "Andean communities living along rivers understand health as a cyclical process — flowing, pooling, returning — rather than a static destination to be achieved and maintained."),
        Quote(q: "Your illness began long before your symptoms. Listen to the earliest whispers.",
